//? Title: Breadth-First Search: FIFO Layers and Minimum-Edge Paths
//? Subtitle: Native queue records, first-discovery predecessors and the cost of recording a frontier
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Breadth-first search removes vertices from a FIFO queue, marking each vertex
when it is first enqueued. That ordering makes every discovered distance a
minimum number of edges from the start. We inspect a small graph's actual
queue and predecessor choices, retain the original three-vertex example,
and distinguish a discovered vertex from one already dequeued. Generated
four-neighbour grids provide a closed-form distance check and exact adjacency
work counts. Path, distance and queue records come from one canonical C++ loop.
)

\toc

> A small graph: the first predecessor fixes the path

Start at vertex zero and seek vertex five. The start enqueues one before two.
They subsequently enqueue three and four, so three is processed first and
claims five's predecessor. When four later reaches five, that vertex is
already marked and is not enqueued again. Both routes have three edges;
the input adjacency order selects path 0–1–3–5 deterministically.

The graph shows that selected path in green. Node distances and every row of
the table are read from the native trace. Queue snapshots show the active FIFO
immediately before removal; discoveries are the new entries appended by that
vertex. The final goal dequeue is included but its successors are not expanded.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/bfs_queue_path.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t,std::size_t>> edges{{0,1},{0,2},{1,3},{2,4},{4,5},{3,5}};
  const auto trace=dm::algorithms::breadth_first_search_trace(6,edges,0,5);
  const std::vector<dm::graphics::DiagramPoint> position{{0,0},{4,1.7},{4,-1.7},{8,1.7},{8,-1.7},{12,0}};
  dm::graphics::Diagram diagram(65,1100);
  for (std::size_t v=0;v<position.size();++v) {
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle style;style.width=1.8;style.height=1.2;
    if (std::find(trace.result.path.begin(),trace.result.path.end(),v)!=trace.result.path.end()) style.fill={220,252,231};
    diagram.node(std::format("v{}",v),position[v],std::format("v{}\nd = {}",v,trace.distance[v]),style);
  }
  for (const auto& [u,v]:edges) {
    bool selected=false;
    for (std::size_t i=1;i<trace.result.path.size();++i)
      if (trace.result.path[i-1]==u && trace.result.path[i]==v) selected=true;
    dm::graphics::DiagramStroke stroke;stroke.color=selected?dm::RGB{22,163,74}:dm::RGB{148,163,184};stroke.width=selected?3:2;
    diagram.edge(std::format("v{}",u),std::format("v{}",v),"",stroke);
  }
  diagram.text({6,-3.4},std::format("minimum-edge path: {}; d counts edges, not vertices",trace.result.path))
      .save_svg("build/bfs_queue_path.svg");
  std::print("| removed vertex | depth | queue before removal | newly enqueued | adjacency entries inspected | goal stop |\n"
             "| ---: | ---: | :--- | :--- | ---: | :--- |\n");
  for (const auto& step:trace.steps)
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",step.vertex,step.depth,step.queue_before,step.discovered,step.edges_examined,step.reached_goal);
  std::print("\nPredecessors: {} (sentinel 6). Layer counts: {}. Maximum queue length: {}.\n",
      trace.predecessor,trace.layer_counts,trace.max_queue_size);
}
```
